  },
  "transformation": {
    "operations": [
      "Measure each pack axis (chrome-cap centre) and trace its right edge per row, top edge per column (clean backdrop sides) and bottom edge per column (first sharp tonal step above the smooth shadow)",
      "Build a symmetric matte by mirroring that traced geometry about the axis (matte geometry only; no pixel is mirrored)",
      "Normalise RGB by the measured backdrop colour (backdrop -> white), as the previous builder did",
      "Keep source pixels inside the matte (proportional Lanczos scale only); discard everything outside (backdrop and the original lower-left studio shadow)",
      "Place every pack on one baseline (y=1020 of 1100) on a 640x1100 canvas, axis centred; heights {'cleanser': 932, 'serum': 858, 'eye': 858, 'cream': 441}",
      "Add one shared synthetic soft contact shadow (two elliptical Gaussian pools, warm graphite, light from upper right)",
      "Left matte edge 0.5px further in than the right, matte feather 0.45px (round 2: matching edge softness)",
      "hxc set: export 320/480/640 px from the 640x1100 master (every pack at <=1.0x its source pixel size)",
      "2:3 set: master x1.0837 composited on 1000x1500 (foot y=1265), export 480/720/960 px",
      "Encode transparent AVIF/WebP; flatten JPEG fallback on RGB 251,250,247"
    ],
    "packaging_geometry_and_label_content_retained": true,
    "literal_product_RGB_pixels_unchanged": false,
    "note": "Product pixels are the supplied packshot pixels after proportional resampling and backdrop normalisation; no repainting, no generative fill, no mirroring of pixels."
  },
